# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers (see wrangler.jsonc: assets.directory = ./public).
# Rules stack: a later matching rule adds to an earlier one, and "! Header" drops what an earlier
# rule set -- so the /js, /css, /icons and /img rules first remove the no-store from /*.
#
# The page shell, the service worker and the manifest must never be cached by the browser -- an
# update has to land the moment it's deployed (the service worker then tells open tabs to refresh).
# Everything under /js and /css is version-stamped in index.html and sw.js (app.js?v=NN,
# style.css?v=NN), so a changed file always has a new URL and the old one can be cached for a year
# as immutable. Icons and art change rarely and get a week.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
/js/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/css/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/icons/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/img/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
